# --- Project-specific: data ---
# data/raw is version-controlled on purpose. Yahoo's adjusted-close history is
# not stable over time (it is restated as new distributions accrue), so a
# re-download months from now would silently change our calibration. Committing
# the exact bytes we calibrated on is what makes the results reproducible.
# data/processed is committed so every table in the report can be audited
# without re-running the pipeline.
# data/interim is a byte-for-byte working copy of data/raw, regenerated by
# clean.py on every run - no reason to store it twice.
data/interim/

# Albert's proposal, adopted (EXPERIMENTS.md §4): commit the small,
# reproducible outputs (the index, manifests, settings, and evaluation/
# folders) so Part V/VI numbers can be reviewed without re-running a
# multi-hour experiment. Keep the large training logs (run_*.npz) local
# only, since the same master seed and code regenerate them exactly.
# `**` catches the logs at any depth, including under a --results-dir
# subfolder. results/smoke*/ holds reduced-settings pipeline checks, which
# are not report results and stay local entirely, as does the runner's
# half-written comparison staging folder (.<name>.new/).
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
!results/INDEX.md
!results/index.json
!results/settings.json
!results/*/
results/**/*.npz
# TC-drift final runs: each seed's theta snapshots and log (about 150 KB) are
# what the scoring and D12 read, so they are committed (William, 2026-11-20).
!results/tc-drift/runs/*/seed*.npz
results/smoke*/
results/.*.new/
# Full-run console logs are small and are the only record of how a
# multi-hour run went (RUN_ISSUES_2026-10-22.md Finding 7), so keep them.
!results/full_run_*.log

# --- R ---
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rapp.history
